{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy","id":521150,"title":"Making Crossover Work for Mummy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-20T02:08:28-07:00","id":521150,"title":"Making Crossover Work for Mummy","content":"By default, <i>Mummy</i> is a game opposed to crossover content. It frames the World of Darkness in an Irem-centric, Arisen-centric manner, and doesn't care much for anything that doesn't fit that paradigm. That's totally fine; this thread isn't for shaking that up. Instead, I want to see what all we can put together from the other lines to enhance all of our Descents with a little bit more spice.<br /> <br /> <i>Vampire</i> has the most natural potential, in my opinion. It's nice to have someone else immortal to share the endless night with, and that the Kindred as a whole have heavy ties to Ancient Egypt. Of particular interest to us here are the Usiri bloodline from <i>Ancient Bloodlines</i>, who cast themselves are the guardians of memories (who would hold onto them while elders slumbered) and shepherds through the terrors of the underworld. We also have the Khaibit (from <i>Bloodlines: the Hidden</i>), who are a group with a sacred purpose of servitude and the ability to see and combat spirits. It may just be me, but the Khaibit seem like they could be the remnants of a Cult, long abandoned and half-remembering their original purpose. The Mnemosyne (<i>Shadows in the Dark - Mekhet</i>) are another bloodline, and these guys have a signature Discipline that revolves around the manipulation of memory.<br /> <br /> Pile onto that the Hollow Mekhet (from <i>Shadows in the Dark - Mekhet</i>), whose Ka explicitly wander around separate from their bodies, and the ever-popular Strix, who seem to be like nothing more than hungry disembodied Sheut, and there's a whole mess of other critters running around for the Arisen to bump into and possibly exploit. There's the oldest Shadow Cult, the Followers of Seth/Cradle of Chaos, who act as agents of pure chaos in the name of maintaining cosmic balance; for the Arisen (who serve the Judges that brought the Law to mankind) they make ready opponents<br /> <br /> I love the idea of a Cult that's at least partially made of vampires, a constant across the Descents who have their own struggles against the Fog of Ages but know loyalty to their Arisen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 05-20-2015, 05:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T05:53:29-07:00","id":521698,"title":"","content":"What makes it opposed to crossover? Not many of the 1e core books spend time on crossover, and few of their supplements come to mind: the big three have enough supplements that can mention other splats (but I can't think of any?) so, of the once-limited lines, <b>Promethean</b> and <b>Changeling</b> are notable exceptions.<br /> <br /> <b>Demon</b>, yes, talks in its core about this stuff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T07:57:45-07:00","id":521884,"title":"","content":"Coming up with story ideas for a crossover is not hard, it's logistics of working in mummies that would be an issue- a character slowly getting weaker instead of stronger and then going to take a dirt nap to recharge.<br /> <br /> Vampire- Theban Sorcery is named that because it comes from Thebes, a lance scholar looking into the origins of their magic might end up researching into relic making and iremite sorcery. <br /> <br /> A mummies cult could come into conflict, or contact with a mekhet blood cult.<br /> <br /> Werewolf- A mummy's cult could recruit a wolf-blood. The mummy's cult might attract spirits, perhaps even a totem. Or a mummy's cultist might become a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Mage- The mysterium research occult secrets,and collect magical oddities, and as of second edition mage orders include not mages, so perhaps there are sorcerers among them. Or perhaps a would be lich decides to study the arisen.<br /> <br /> Promethean- Osirans are quite possibly an attempt at arisen 2.0. Since human demiurges is even more of a thing in second edition, a mummy looking for a sorcerer might find he has an osiran friend for protection.<br /> <br /> Changeling- Perhaps a mummy's cultist is a fetch the changeling is going for, there is a changeling entitlement of cult leaders, so again cult on cult conflict possibilities.<br /> <br /> Hunter- AO, Aegis, Cheiron, Barret Commision, these guys would be on mummies like white on rice. Do the keepers of the source sense sekhem? Did the promethean brotherhood stumble upon iremite sorcery? <br /> <br /> Demon- A demon could have an identity as a mummy cultist, or perhaps a demon with an identity of a ghost runs across a mummy.<br /> <br /> Geist- An easy one. Necromancy and egypt go together and peanut butter and chocolate. Both deal with ghosts, so there's that. Both form cults, so there's that. Heck, a sin-eater's geist might have been a mummy's cultist in life, and the mummy's servant in death. <br /> <br /> And beast, beast is all about crossovers.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T11:53:09-07:00","id":522152,"title":"","content":"I can (and have!) written an essay on the weird parallels between the temakh and Geists, and the implied similarities between the Shan'iatu's goal and what I think the fate of a Tier 3 krewe is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T14:09:22-07:00","id":522493,"title":"","content":"Mummy does crossover more like Vampire than, say, Mage. Vampire doesn't go out of its way to make room for anybody else. The room is there, but the game concentrates on its own themes and worldview. That integrity is a big part of what Mummy is about. As a 1e game it treats ghosts as a common resource (as they were in 1e) but otherwise, the presentation is always Mummy-first. I mean, I think I have an idea of where or what Duat might be defined as in another line, but in Mummy it's Duat, and its description in Mummy is the most accurate, and it's not &quot;really&quot; anything else. There might be common territory, but nobody has a better map than anybody else.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T15:41:42-07:00","id":522602,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the accusations of Mummy not being crossover friendly always puzzled me. It presents the game from the Mummy worldview, but there are definitely elements written with crossover in mind. Rebuke the Vizier is probably the biggest example. Tier 3 uses all of its text on examples to describe how it works on Vampires and Mages, without bothering to address how it effects Arisen mechanics at all (which is really, really annoying given that it might, or might not, be able to effect boosted attributes, Sealing the Flesh, and Affinities to some extent, but how isn't discussed because it wants to spend its time talking about Disciplines...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T01:33:40-07:00","id":525268,"title":"","content":"New information regarding Mage/Mummy crossovers. The recent blog 'To The Strongest', has clarified which Arcana transpires to which Piller. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"37\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Ab</td> <td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Spirit</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"37\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Ba</td> <td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Mind</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"37\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Ka</td> <td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Prime</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"37\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Ren</td> <td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Fate</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"37\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Sheut</td> <td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Death</td> </tr> </table></div> The Weret-Hekau even have a section on Mummy crossovers.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Those Who Cross Over</b><br /> As stewards of one of the world\u2019s oldest civilizations and skilled record keepers, the Weret-Hekau have accumulated a significant amount of information about supernatural beings who have interfered in their nation\u2019s history. Unfortunately Hemka are not immune to internal rivalries, so to dig anything up, a sorcerer needs to trade favors for access to a library or talkative expert.<br /> A disciplined seeker of the truth would discover that after the fall of the Scorpion quasi-dynasty their creations, Arisen as detailed in <b>Mummy: The Curse</b>, dragged themselves out of the sand during the reign of Unas, sparking a conflict that drove most of them from the region and hurled Kemet into chaos. Few Arisen have been seen since, but lesser (though dangerous) entities called Shuankhsen can still be found hidden among the populace. Weret-Hekau believe these beings are the result of incautious experiments with Sekhem. In contemporary terms, Sekhem is not \u201cSupernal,\u201d but the stuff of existence as it actually manifests. Awakened magic interacts with it like a smith holding tongs, while the Predynastic ancients preferred to grab this molten stuff with the spiritual equivalent of their bare hands. Weret-Hekau do not necessarily believe the works of Irem (a name few of them know) to be evil, but dangerous. Hemka have attempted to learn the old arts before, but progressing beyond elementary knowledge . . . damages them. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T01:46:32-07:00","id":525291,"title":"","content":"Glad to know the Awakened view the Nameless Empire as it was; fueled by batshit insane geniuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T02:32:14-07:00","id":548175,"title":"","content":"And now we have <i>Beast</i> to play with.<br /> <br /> Anyone else thinking about having one of the Begotten as a tomb guardian or high priestess?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T07:12:18-07:00","id":548471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=548175#post548175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now we have <i>Beast</i> to play with.<br /> <br /> Anyone else thinking about having one of the Begotten as a tomb guardian or high priestess?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;WHERE THE FUCK IS MY TOMB!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;WHAT THE HELL IS THIS PLACE?! <br /> <br /> &quot;WHAT IN THE NAME OF THE JUDGES IS THAT!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>krrrrrrraaaaaaannnnngggg!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T07:38:36-07:00","id":548543,"title":"","content":"I don't know, seems more likely they'd go &quot;AMKHAT! DIE!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T08:59:55-07:00","id":548746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=548175#post548175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now we have <i>Beast</i> to play with.<br /> <br /> Anyone else thinking about having one of the Begotten as a tomb guardian or high priestess?</div> </div> </div> </div>High Priestess? Sin-Eater. Tomb Guardian? Abso-freaking-lutely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:22:18-07:00","id":548793,"title":"","content":"How would people rule the interaction between the Deceived's material anchoring and the effects of opening a Primordial Pathway, incidentally?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:34:49-07:00","id":548811,"title":"","content":"Extremely uncomfortable for the Deceived. On top of that, a Deceived juststraight up can't crossover, and will never run the risk of being spirited away. Being in the presence of a Pathway to a lair, the two worlds overlapping, feels like being dashed against the rocks-enough that I'd say they'd take penalties to actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T16:53:43-07:00","id":549517,"title":"","content":"Just on a personal level, I have some idle notes combining Mummy with Vampire, Geist, Promethean and Inferno demons. In particular, I like to think that the Strix and the Inferno demons were some of the horrid creatures that that the Shan'iatu had to contend with while building their Empire (well, actually in my personal notes the Shan'iatu might have ripped holes in the cosmos to let them out into the world in the first place, but those notes were written pre-BotDeceived, so the nature of the Shan'iatu is much different than canon's).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T16:59:31-07:00","id":549520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=549517#post549517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just on a personal level, I have some idle notes combining Mummy with Vampire, Geist, Promethean and Inferno demons. In particular, I like to think that the Strix and the Inferno demons were some of the horrid creatures that that the Shan'iatu had to contend with while building their Empire (well, actually in my personal notes the Shan'iatu might have ripped holes in the cosmos to let them out into the world in the first place, but those notes were written pre-BotDeceived, so the nature of the Shan'iatu is much different than canon's).</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully believe that the Strix are (at least, to an Arisen understanding) are a Sheut divorced from the other fifths of the soul and let loose. As for Geist, I've written some gigantic tumblr posts explaining how I think that the Shan'iatu were basically a krewe, simply made of not-humans and on a much larger scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T23:10:00-07:00","id":551148,"title":"","content":"Mummies seem to be in an odd place in a crossover with Beasts. I mean, Mummies <i>know</i> their origins. It's possible for them to remember them. For Deceived, it's even possible to recall their Temakh's origins. And unless the Dark Mother is Fate, which Beast... does not really support, there's no obvious familial connection there. Or maybe the Dark Mother is Ammut, and their kinship is actually with the Shuankhsen? Given the origin of the Rite of Return, that might work.<br /> <br /> I do sort of like the mental image of an Arisen and Beast squaring off in a &quot;my origin story is truer than yours&quot; argument.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I don't see an Arisen meret being a good family for the Beast. They're awake far too rarely for the Beast to really benefit, maybe only rising once or twice in the Beast's entire lifetime. And a Lair based in a Tomb (probably the best advantage for a Beast) would probably not be something the Arisen would approve of. Being woken up by wandering Heroes on a regular basis is more likely to irritate the Arisen, and Beasts don't offer a lot in return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T01:02:43-07:00","id":552684,"title":"","content":"Mummies do have some powers that can be quite crossover-friendly, if you're inclined to go that way. For instance, a mummy with the Godsight Affinity can potentially spot and sort-of identify basically any kind of supernatural creature or effect, while the 1 dot Text called <i>The Guruwari Record </i>tends to turn the heads of <i>every</i> supernatural creature in the immediate area when it is activated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T02:54:54-07:00","id":552780,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any good ideas for Changeling crossover? I can make everything else work, but just don't see any easy ties beyond the tenuous connection that Wyrd and Fate may be the same force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T09:10:48-07:00","id":553131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=552780#post552780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have any good ideas for Changeling crossover? I can make everything else work, but just don't see any easy ties beyond the tenuous connection that Wyrd and Fate may be the same force.</div> </div> </div> </div>Subtle Bazaar and whatever you can parley out of the fact that the Ruinous Prince is the same entity who appeared to the mages of Alexander's time as Set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T10:33:44-07:00","id":555841,"title":"","content":"Hawthorn ran a <b>Mummy</b>/<b>Changeling</b> game so PMing him for ideas might be good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T00:09:21-07:00","id":556640,"title":"","content":"Well as I mentioned earlier- A changeling might go after a fetch that's in a mummy's cult.<br /> <br /> Members of the lost pantheon have cults worshipping them, so a changeling and a mummy might find their cults squabbling.<br /> <br /> Also, the Lord Sages of the unknown reaches are an entitlement all about crossovers, they even have the ability to pick up the magic items of other supernaturals such as werewolf fetishes and mage's enhanced items. Wouldn't be much of a stretch to throw in mummy relics too, especially if mummy relics and reliquary relics are the same thing, as I believe.<br /> <br /> Viziers don't age, so a mummy and a vizier might be really old friends, rivals, or enemies. <br /> <br /> A mummy's cult might mistake a token for a relic, bringing changelings and a mummy into conflict.<br /> <br /> A mummy's cultist might be drawn into the hedge to become a fae touched mortal.<br /> <br /> The autumn court is all about occult secrets and fear, mummies provide plenty of both.<br /> <br /> Mummies have ghost cultists, gravewrights can see ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T01:00:20-07:00","id":556663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=521884#post521884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Coming up with story ideas for a crossover is not hard, it's logistics of working in mummies that would be an issue- a character slowly getting weaker instead of stronger and then going to take a dirt nap to recharge.</div> </div> </div> </div>The more I think about it the more I like the idea of playing a mummy in a version of the NWoD where the Sothic Turn happened a few years earlier. The mummy has been awake for a few years now, starts the game at a stable Sekhem 1 (and a mostly uninvolved Cult) and <i>really doesn't want to die</i> as that would take away its chance to really delve into the world and find out stuff about its past.<br /> Though even at Sekhem 1 a Mummy can do some seriously terrifying stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T01:48:40-07:00","id":556677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=556663#post556663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The more I think about it the more I like the idea of playing a mummy in a version of the NWoD where the Sothic Turn happened a few years earlier. The mummy has been awake for a few years now, starts the game at a stable Sekhem 1 (and a mostly uninvolved Cult) and <i>really doesn't want to die</i> as that would take away its chance to really delve into the world and find out stuff about its past.<br /> Though even at Sekhem 1 a Mummy can do some seriously terrifying stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming the Sothic Turn is in 2012, 2014-2015 is perfectly on time frame for allowing that to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T20:36:00-07:00","id":563690,"title":"","content":"I posted this in the Requiem Homebrew Hub thread and thought it was relevant here also: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B5D9AgFEhGZ3cm93Z3JLS29fbGs/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">link.</a><br /> <br /> It's a Mekhet Bloodline centered around serving Mummies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T02:23:06-07:00","id":576243,"title":"","content":"What would be the outcome in a full blown cross over game where someone wanted to play a mummy in a totally mixed group? <br /> <br /> Is it posable to just have their potency stat start low and work higher and give them a bit more freedom with what they choose to do in their unlife? <br /> Posable have them not regain willpower every day they are not working at their intended purpose or something els?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T02:25:34-07:00","id":576244,"title":"","content":"I'm asking as I have a group and no one likes the same thing. So often any WoD game involves a minumum of three supernatural. <br /> I will end up with a Mummy(probably), a Mage, a Werewolf, a Changling and a Demon the Fallen(thanks to conversion guid). <br /> And of course now I'm so hoping like hell the new Mage 2e drops soon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T04:23:33-07:00","id":576265,"title":"","content":"If you want a &quot;start low and build up&quot; progression for a Mummy, you might consider making them a Mummy who has achieved Apotheosis. It allows them to treat their Memory as their power stat, although it does restrict them from the more powerful Utterances. If you have the character begin at Memory 1, presumably having just experienced some serious calamity to have dropped them from the Memory 7 they would have needed, then they can build up alongside the rest of the group while also rediscovering who they are and what befell them to drop them to such depths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T18:19:41-07:00","id":576962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=555841#post555841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hawthorn ran a <b>Mummy</b>/<b>Changeling</b> game</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed I did. It did not end well, but I blame that on my own flaws as an ST my...complex relationship with the source material, a unbalanced group dynamic and my own &quot;meh&quot; feeling towards the Changeling line. <br /> <br /> Anyway...<br /> <br /> I felt the grounding of such a crossover was in the theme of Identity.<br /> <br /> After all Changeling are well...changed by their time in Arcadia. While they come back to our world, they are never really the same again, nor will they ever be &quot;the same&quot; again. Mummy meanwhile is concerned with the rediscovery of identity through the return of a character Memory. <br /> <br /> Apart from that I had a link between Fate and the Wyrd in a sorta &quot;solid state vs liquid state&quot; frame. <br /> <br /> In more specific sense I had a couple of points of interest between the two games StSword pointed some of these out:<br /> <br /> I had a couple of Lord Sages who were looking into Arisen phenomena but had no idea Mummy's existed when the game started. <br /> <br /> I had a Vizier who was really, really old (as in he had been around since the last Sothic Turn) who was the high priest to a Su-Menet Arisen NPC. He had a complex relationship split between his loyalty to the Freehold (which he believed in), his Arisen &quot;master&quot; (who he massively resented for basically being an immortal dick) and his former Keeper (and ex-lover). <br /> <br /> Apart from that I tied a lot of meta-plot in my game to origins points between both games. Having the Shan'Iatu and True Fae (who were also originally human sorcerers who had overthrown the original &quot;gods&quot; of Acardia) be old enemies with lots of treaties and oaths. Ammut and the Tanglewoman being aspects of a larger destructive force that both factions were opposed too. The Heretic being linked to Ruinious Prince. The Decieved being deliberately created by the Judges (who were ascended Shan'Iatu in my game - this was before any of the splat books came out) to fight the True Fae (as they could &quot;see&quot; their true names). <br /> <br /> I kept Tokens and Relics very distinct on purpose. Tokens were much more common and had no really use to Mummy's. Relics were rarer had more pronounced effects and snarled up the Wyrd a bit for Changelings. Vestiges could be drained for glamour though. <br /> <br /> That's the points off the top of my head. Basically, with Mummy for me its always going back to Irem and working out how much you want to tie the other supernaturals to that point of origin. The Fae were only tangentally related (not from Irem or made by the Shan'Iatu) but they interacted with the metaphysics of the wider setting and therefore were something that the Shan'Iatu had to take into account. So this is not to say everything has to originate in Irem merely you have to consider how it might have interacted with Irem (if it did at all, if its a newer phenomena, meaning it was not factored into the Shan'Iatu's plots)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T01:19:40-07:00","id":577136,"title":"","content":"I ran a game not too long ago where I had three players.<br /> <br /> The first player was a mummy.<br /> The second was a vampire who was part of the &quot;Children of Osiris&quot;* group.<br /> The third and final player player was a osirion promethean.<br /> <br /> It was a blast from what me and my players recalled.<br /> <br /> *: Brownie points for anyone who remembers who or what the Children of Osiris is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5554-psychic_monkey","name":"Psychic_Monkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T06:17:34-07:00","id":577289,"title":"","content":"Man, Hawthorn, I remember reading about your group's sessions but in this post here you really sound like you had planned everything just right","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T05:34:45-08:00","id":802996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=525268#post525268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New information regarding Mage/Mummy crossovers. The recent blog 'To The Strongest', has clarified which Arcana transpires to which Piller. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"37\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Ab</td> <td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Spirit</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"37\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Ba</td> <td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Mind</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"37\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Ka</td> <td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Prime</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"37\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Ren</td> <td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Fate</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"37\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Sheut</td> <td width=\"44\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 2px\">Death</td> </tr> </table></div> The Weret-Hekau even have a section on Mummy crossovers.</div> </div> </div> </div> You mind linking me to this specific post on the blog? Or is it something found in the Kickstarter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T06:01:16-08:00","id":803014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=802996#post802996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You mind linking me to this specific post on the blog? Or is it something found in the Kickstarter?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/going-back-in-time-mage-the-awakening-dark-eras/\" target=\"_blank\">Weret-Hekau magic places all phenomena under the dominion of the gods and the five parts of the human soul.</a>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T06:43:40-08:00","id":803042,"title":"","content":"Whoa.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That definitely got me thinking. What if there's a present day Nameless Order that bears the name of the Weret-Hekau and considers itself a revival of that old tradition? Just a curious possibility, seeing as we don't have any named Nameless Orders so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T07:57:59-08:00","id":803090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=803042#post803042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...seeing as we don't have any named Nameless Orders so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw this and thought &quot;that's because they are <i>Nameless</i>&quot;, though I know that isn't accurate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T11:44:34-08:00","id":803236,"title":"","content":"I can see the heirs of the Weret-Hekau as a Legacy sooner than as a Nameless Order, but I'd happily play as one of either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:33:45-08:00","id":803441,"title":"","content":"I've always thought that a Mummy with an Usiri Bloodline servant would make a lot of sense. No idea as to whether their special Discipline would even work on an Arisen in <i>henet </i>but it would be amazing if it did. Sin-Eaters, of course, fit perfectly with Mummies. I'm just imagining a Sin-Eater who can actually travel to the Underworld and visit Polydegmon, while also serving in the Mummy cult that was implied to be behind the Necromanteion in ancient Greece in Sothis Ascends.<br /> <br /> A thought that occurred to me while rereading Geist is that the Shan'iatu did a whole lot of experimenting with souls, and seem to have a unilateral view of Twilight. Who's to say they didn't <i>create </i>a few <i>geister </i>during their experimental diaspora? And more importantly, the Su-Menet just <i>scream </i>Tier 3 Krewe at me. A very, very small number of their member were probably Bound, for obvious reasons, but it makes far too much sense, and it allows for a really awesome Bronze Age Chronicle with some creative work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:41:18-08:00","id":803447,"title":"","content":"I'll do you one further and say the the Deceived are essentially Sin-Eaters, but while Geists are born of human dead, their Temakh are whatever is left of dead/shattered Shan'iatu. Mummy has a lot of Geist crossover potential in general; one might even say that Duat is one of the deepest Dead Dominions, past the River of Blood described in Dreams of Avarice.<br /> <br /> All of the Egyptian stuff for Vampire - the Khaibit, the Usiri, the Cult of Seth - all make fantastic Mummy NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:56:09-08:00","id":803455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=803441#post803441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always thought that a Mummy with an Usiri Bloodline servant would make a lot of sense. No idea as to whether their special Discipline would even work on an Arisen in <i>henet </i>but it would be amazing if it did. Sin-Eaters, of course, fit perfectly with Mummies. I'm just imagining a Sin-Eater who can actually travel to the Underworld and visit Polydegmon, while also serving in the Mummy cult that was implied to be behind the Necromanteion in ancient Greece in Sothis Ascends.<br /> <br /> A thought that occurred to me while rereading Geist is that the Shan'iatu did a whole lot of experimenting with souls, and seem to have a unilateral view of Twilight. Who's to say they didn't <i>create </i>a few <i>geister </i>during their experimental diaspora? And more importantly, the Su-Menet just <i>scream </i>Tier 3 Krewe at me. A very, very small number of their member were probably Bound, for obvious reasons, but it makes far too much sense, and it allows for a really awesome Bronze Age Chronicle with some creative work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of the Usiri, I might actually make a 2E Adaptation of them (and the Bak-Ra perhaps, too). I completely forget about them, until now.<br /> <br /> And Geist isn't the only other line that can crossover smoothly with Mummy. There's also Promethean, too, especially if the Su-Menet conducted experiments which gave rise perhaps to predecessors/prototypes of what would become the Osiran Lineage/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:06:39-08:00","id":803463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=803455#post803455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of the Usiri, I might actually make a 2E Adaptation of them (and the Bak-Ra perhaps, too). I completely forget about them, until now.<br /> <br /> And Geist isn't the only other line that can crossover smoothly with Mummy. There's also Promethean, too, especially if the Su-Menet conducted experiments which gave rise perhaps to predecessors/prototypes of what would become the Osiran Lineage/</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be ecstatic if you updated the Usiri.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:19:45-08:00","id":803473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=803455#post803455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also Promethean, too, especially if the Su-Menet conducted experiments which gave rise perhaps to predecessors/prototypes of what would become the Osiran Lineage/</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh.<br /> <br /> *looks at Azar*<br /> <br /> Sort of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T20:32:53-08:00","id":803539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=803447#post803447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll do you one further and say the the Deceived are essentially Sin-Eaters, but while Geists are born of human dead, their Temakh are whatever is left of dead/shattered Shan'iatu. Mummy has a lot of Geist crossover potential in general; one might even say that Duat is one of the deepest Dead Dominions, past the River of Blood described in Dreams of Avarice.<br /> <br /> All of the Egyptian stuff for Vampire - the Khaibit, the Usiri, the Cult of Seth - all make fantastic Mummy NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love all of this. Ah, so Duat actually is in the Underworld; I've always wondered. That makes me terribly excited to get my hands on this book- I love lore, it's some of the best story inspiration, and Mummy has some truly glorious lore.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it be amazing for a bunch of Sin-Eaters to dive deep enough and find Irem? The actual city, transported to the Underworld. A place where the living, impossibly, still serve their god - kings thousands of years later, generations born knowing only the light of torches, and the Phlogiston River. Unbreakable walls guarded by bound ghosts and worse, unassailable against the forces of the Deathlords and Kerberoi. And here's the kicker. The Shan'iatu still own their servants. All that Sekhem? Their souls still craft it into wonders, relics that will never see the light of day except, perhaps, as mysterious relics from the gods or the Judges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T05:18:59-08:00","id":803674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=803539#post803539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love all of this. Ah, so Duat actually is in the Underworld; I've always wondered. That makes me terribly excited to get my hands on this book- I love lore, it's some of the best story inspiration, and Mummy has some truly glorious lore.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it be amazing for a bunch of Sin-Eaters to dive deep enough and find Irem? The actual city, transported to the Underworld. A place where the living, impossibly, still serve their god - kings thousands of years later, generations born knowing only the light of torches, and the Phlogiston River. Unbreakable walls guarded by bound ghosts and worse, unassailable against the forces of the Deathlords and Kerberoi. And here's the kicker. The Shan'iatu still own their servants. All that Sekhem? Their souls still craft it into wonders, relics that will never see the light of day except, perhaps, as mysterious relics from the gods or the Judges.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can already expect people who weave translated CWoD concepts into Chronicles of Darkness to try and make Irem of the Pillars a Dead Dominion inspired somewhat by Amenti, the Dark Kingdom of Sand.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd like to add in the possibility that perhaps the living residents of the city might have a large percentage of Sin-Eaters among their number. It wouldn't be a stretch to imagine the Shan'iatu having geists among their legions of enslaved ghosts, and forcing several of them to strike a Bargain upon some of their subjects.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=803463#post803463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be ecstatic if you updated the Usiri.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803717-bloodline-usiri\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803717-bloodline-usiri\"> Bloodline: Usiri - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803717-bloodline-usiri\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/803717-bloodline-usiri </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Crook and the Flail Usiri Parent Clan: Nosferatu Nickname: Judges Disciplines: Auspex, Nightmare, Obfuscate, Vigor You are hereby found guilty of treason and </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And I believe I may have done exactly that.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Enjoy my reinterpretation of the bloodline. Critique is deeply appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-08-2016, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T08:44:14-08:00","id":803770,"title":"","content":"I'll comment on the Usiri later, but you do realize this discussion is eventually going to lead to a single logical conclusion, yeah? One or both of us making Irem as a Dead Dominion. Which would be awesome and utterly insane in all the right ways, I think. What would a Slaughterer be like in the Underworld, I wonder? Some kind of Cthonian?<br /> <br /> According to the Demon Storytellers Guide section on Sin-Eaters, the Underworld is broken. Huh. I <i>wonder </i>what could have done that? Maybe a certain jackal-headed Deathlord really should be down there instead of wandering Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 01-08-2016, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T10:20:29-08:00","id":803825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=803770#post803770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll comment on the Usiri later, but you do realize this discussion is eventually going to lead to a single logical conclusion, yeah? One or both of us making Irem as a Dead Dominion. Which would be awesome and utterly insane in all the right ways, I think. What would a Slaughterer be like in the Underworld, I wonder? Some kind of Cthonian?</div> </div> </div> </div>And then there's the matter of the Shan'iatu. Who are very likely Duat's equivalent of the Kerberoi found in other (more 'conventional') Dead Dominions.<br /> <br /> Yes. One or the other doing a write-up of Irem would be the <i>only</i> logical conclusion to this discussion. Hey. Maybe it could even be a collaborative effort, one that could have other people pitch in as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=803770#post803770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the Demon Storytellers Guide section on Sin-Eaters, the Underworld is broken. Huh. I <i>wonder </i>what could have done that? Maybe a certain jackal-headed Deathlord really should be down there instead of wandering Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. You just made Demon Storyteller's Guide <i>another </i>addition to the list of books/pdfs I'd like to get somehow but can't at the moment do to having no way of acquiring it. Topping even the Demon Translation Guide and soon to equal (when they're out) Mage 2E and Dark Eras in terms of anticipation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-08-2016, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T14:09:09-08:00","id":803987,"title":"","content":"I would totally agree with doing a collaborative write up of Duat as a utterly vast Dead Dominion. The crossover write up is interesting for several reasons, not the least of which is that it also gives the bare bones for a simplistic Geist 2E conversion, and specifically calls out Kerberoi as Spirits as opposed to Ghosts, which is really weird. They are specifically called out as having two Bans as opposed to a Ban and a Bane- Punish those who break the Old Laws, and never leave the Underworld. They are described as judges and jailers- the 'eternally dead' -and are always Rank 5 no matter how deep the Dead Dominion is.<br /> <br /> What I'm wondering is, where the heck are Azar and Aset? Because they were sent to the Great Below. Do they rule a second Dead Dominion near Irem? Are the Judges of Death all exceptionally powerful Kerberoi verging on Deathlords? Is Ammut the thing causing the Underworld's gravity? So many questions, but one thing I'm almost sure of- Anpu used to be a load-bearing member of the Great Below, and Azar is probably not working out as a replacement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T20:35:06-08:00","id":804236,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my theory has always been to place Duat beneath the Ocean of Fragments, and attribute the memory-destroying aspects of the Rite of Return to a bug (or possibly a feature?) resulting from having to pass through the Ocean. The Rite protects their identity, but only just enough to get them there and back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T21:03:10-08:00","id":804243,"title":"","content":"Hmm... how would the River of Blood be down there then? Unless a tributary branches off the Ocean and goes deeper? How many Rivers down is the Ocean of Fragments anyways?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T22:04:00-08:00","id":804253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=804243#post804243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... how would the River of Blood be down there then? Unless a tributary branches off the Ocean and goes deeper? How many Rivers down is the Ocean of Fragments anyways?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall, it's at the &quot;bottom&quot; in that nobody's gotten past it and returned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T22:09:04-08:00","id":804254,"title":"","content":"The Ocean of Fragments is past <i>all</i> the rivers, and the only thing past the Ocean is oblivion.<br /> <br /> Er, not that Oblivion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T22:11:06-08:00","id":804256,"title":"","content":"Right, so, if Duat is in the Underworld it must be on the banks of the River of Blood at some point before the Ocean of Fragments","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T23:05:46-08:00","id":804266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=803987#post803987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would totally agree with doing a collaborative write up of Duat as a utterly vast Dead Dominion. The crossover write up is interesting for several reasons, not the least of which is that it also gives the bare bones for a simplistic Geist 2E conversion, and specifically calls out Kerberoi as Spirits as opposed to Ghosts, which is really weird. They are specifically called out as having two Bans as opposed to a Ban and a Bane- Punish those who break the Old Laws, and never leave the Underworld. They are described as judges and jailers- the 'eternally dead' -and are always Rank 5 no matter how deep the Dead Dominion is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sent the link by P.M then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Anybody else who's interested, just send me a note.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-09-2016, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T04:02:56-08:00","id":804341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=804254#post804254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ocean of Fragments is past <i>all</i> the rivers, and the only thing past the Ocean is oblivion.<br /> <br /> Er, not that Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that we'd know, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T05:51:42-08:00","id":804396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=804256#post804256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, so, if Duat is in the Underworld it must be on the banks of the River of Blood at some point before the Ocean of Fragments</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could you elaborate the bit on the River of Blood for me?<br /> <br /> But yeah. Speaking of Rivers, I would have thought that the River of Memory (Lethe) and perhaps even the River of Lamentation (Cocytus) would have better fit for an Egyptian-themed Dead Dominion. Or even Sinaan, the River of Scorpions.<br /> <br /> ... Unless perhaps Duat isn't simply just <i>one</i> Dead Dominion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-09-2016, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T06:07:15-08:00","id":804405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=804396#post804396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Could you elaborate the bit on the River of Blood for me?<br /> <br /> But yeah. Speaking of Rivers, I would have thought that the River of Memory (Lethe) and perhaps even the River of Lamentation (Cocytus) would have better fit for an Egyptian-themed Dead Dominion. Or even Sinaan, the River of Scorpions.<br /> <br /> ... Unless perhaps Duat isn't simply just <i>one</i> Dead Dominion?</div> </div> </div> </div> The further down you go, the more Rivers you have to pass. Who says Duat isn't past all of these, and just happens to end up on the banks of one of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T06:09:08-08:00","id":804406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=803987#post803987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would totally agree with doing a collaborative write up of Duat as a utterly vast Dead Dominion. The crossover write up is interesting for several reasons, not the least of which is that it also gives the bare bones for a simplistic Geist 2E conversion, and specifically calls out Kerberoi as Spirits as opposed to Ghosts, which is really weird. They are specifically called out as having two Bans as opposed to a Ban and a Bane- Punish those who break the Old Laws, and never leave the Underworld. They are described as judges and jailers- the 'eternally dead' -and are always Rank 5 no matter how deep the Dead Dominion is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is odd, because Kerberoi are supposed to be Rank 6+ Ghosts...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T08:25:14-08:00","id":804468,"title":"","content":"Unless Kerberoi are Cthonians and thus ghosts of things that never really lived? Or the word was used in a general manner, since it wasn't capitalized? Is it still canon that Geists are ghost/spirit hybrids? Maybe a Kerberos, to an extent, is the Dominion itself, and the being most people interact with is a Rank 5 Royal Avatar?<br /> <br /> Maybe Duat, like Mictlan/Hades in Book of the Dead, is a Dead Dominion that can only be found by trying to reach it, and the unique path to reach it is itself part of the realm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T08:34:35-08:00","id":804477,"title":"","content":"We should keep in mind that DSG contains hacks for other lines, not guarantees. It could just be that that's how they chose to emulate Kerberoi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T08:43:40-08:00","id":804481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=804468#post804468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless Kerberoi are Cthonians and thus ghosts of things that never really lived? Or the word was used in a general manner, since it wasn't capitalized? Is it still canon that Geists are ghost/spirit hybrids? Maybe a Kerberos, to an extent, is the Dominion itself, and the being most people interact with is a Rank 5 Royal Avatar?<br /> <br /> Maybe Duat, like Mictlan/Hades in Book of the Dead, is a Dead Dominion that can only be found by trying to reach it, and the unique path to reach it is itself part of the realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still thinking that geists <i>are</i> ghost/spirit hybrids, considering how changed they are from their original existence as ghosts. As for the matter of Rank 6+ Kerberoi, I think I can agree with your idea that they could communicate with people via an Avatar. Of course, that still leaves entities like the Kerberos of the Ocean of Fragments. But that's an entirely different story.<br /> <br /> On Duat, I imagine it's even more difficult to reach than Mictlan, especially when you consider the fact that <i>Irem</i> was transported there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T08:48:33-08:00","id":804485,"title":"","content":"There's probably a long set of complicated rituals involved. The idea of coating Egyptian tombs in spells to ensure travel to Duat had to start somewhere in the CofD. Also, yeah, probably taking the STG too literally- but it's the only real 2e guidelines for the Underworld until Dark Eras comes out and we find out what the Border Marches, the Shadow, and the Underworld were like back before Irem and the Sundering Before it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 01-09-2016, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T09:11:20-08:00","id":804495,"title":"","content":"True that.<br /> <br /> Although I have to point out, now, one little tidbit for addressing a Geist/Mummy Crossover. The Dead Dominion of Mictlan has en entity that's identified as <i>Anubis. </i>And yet Anpu is described in the Mummy books as being an entity found only in the Neter-Khetet (Twilight). Any idea on how to explain it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T09:30:21-08:00","id":804501,"title":"","content":"Well, the CofD are really weird- most mythic figures likely have more than one incarnation. You've got various Major Templates emulating or inspiring stories, the True Fae patterning themselves off myths, spirits born from resonance from sacrifice and worship, and the Goetic beings that stem purely from human thought.<br /> <br /> The Astral Realm of Death is said to have Verges or Gates leading to the Underworld. Maybe Mictlan Anubis is the Astral one, or maybe the Lord of Mictlan just liked the aesthtic. Anpu was almost certainly a load bearing Deathlord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T17:50:18-08:00","id":804857,"title":"","content":"I was somewhat surprised after a lot of hints that Duat was in the Lower Depths. Though it's been ages since I read the Underworld book so I don't know how much overlap if any those places can have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T18:25:37-08:00","id":804882,"title":"","content":"I always figured that 'beneath' the Ocean of Fragments was Oblivion (yes, that one) and that, in this 'verse, Oblivion is a Lower Depth. Or that Oblivion is a synonym for the Lower Depths, or vice versa.<br /> <br /> Basically, swim beyond the Ocean of Fragments, which is in the Underworld, and find Duat, which is a Lower Depth of which is Oblivion. Or something","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T19:17:55-08:00","id":804924,"title":"","content":"The Dead Dominions are sometimes called the Lower Depths, but I don't think they're the same as Mage's Lower Depths. Maybe if something is expelled from the Ocean early it falls to a Lower Depth- whatever trait is missing dictates which Lower Depth it falls into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T20:16:45-08:00","id":804954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=804924#post804924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dead Dominions are sometimes called the Lower Depths</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=422364#post422364\">No they're not</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T20:21:48-08:00","id":804962,"title":"","content":"Ah, thank-you. That's what I get for not cracking open a book before posting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T20:22:31-08:00","id":804963,"title":"","content":"Quick note: Mummy's cosmology doesn't care about the Underworld. Duat lies beyond the horizon of mortal Twilight. Curse, in general, is concerned with Twilight as the passing place of the dead rather than the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T20:35:34-08:00","id":804972,"title":"","content":"Well now- that's a Mystery a Mage could pursue for their entire life. Which is why I should probably quit trying to map Duat while I'm still ahead. Will still probably make it a Dead Dominion just for fun, but no chance of that being anything close to canon.<br /> <br /> Next thing you're going to tell me is that Duat is a place between Twilight and the Underworld the way the Hedge is a place between earth and Arcadia and the Border Marches used to be the passage from Earth to the Shadow. Nah- probably a crazy idea. Dark Eras can't come quick enough. I need the Bird and the Bull to figure out what weirdness was going on pre-Sundering and pre-Irem","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T20:40:36-08:00","id":804977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=804972#post804972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well now- that's a Mystery a Mage could pursue for their entire life. Which is why I should probably quit trying to map Duat while I'm still ahead. Will still probably make it a Dead Dominion just for fun, but no chance of that being anything close to canon.<br /> <br /> Next thing you're going to tell me is that Duat is a place between Twilight and the Underworld the way the Hedge is a place between earth and Arcadia and the Border Marches used to be the passage from Earth to the Shadow. Nah- probably a crazy idea. Dark Eras can't come quick enough. I need the Bird and the Bull to figure out what weirdness was going on pre-Sundering and pre-Irem</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be absurd; /everyone/ knows the Underworld is the Fallen reflection of Stygia!<br /> <br /> Seriously, Mage cosmology is a rabbit hole with no escape, and bringing crossover into it just makes people upset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T20:51:03-08:00","id":804983,"title":"","content":"I think maybe that's the idea with Mage? Hubris, Supernal Truth, etc. Only problem is it carries over to the readers, instead of staying on the page. And I'd probably be that Free Council jerk saying &quot;How do we know Stygia isn't a perfected image of the Underworld?&quot; I didn't mean to try and go down the Mage rabbit hole, but at least we backed out of it.<br /> <br /> Running Mummies in &quot;To the Strongest&quot; would be a ball, I think, thanks to the Egyptian Great Cult whose name I can't remember right now.<br /> <br /> The idea that Duat is somehow 'beyond' Twilight really intrigues me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T21:08:06-08:00","id":804990,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that we're getting Mummy/Mage crossover in the Mutapa Era.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I'm in love with the Weret-Hekau. The same blog entry also mentions something fun re: Mummy:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In an Egyptian palace of red stone, Sopdet (Sothis), manifestation of Aset (Isis) and queen of Time, stands by an empty throne. The crown of Upper Egypt sits upon it, darkened by the shadow of some snouted predatory beast. Sopdet explains that her co-regent, Set of Fate, is not bound to the end of worlds like the others. She represents both of them in the palace of the Acanthos. </div> </div> </div>Set/Sutek, the Suzugoi of Fate, is either absent or roaming the cosmos with impunity. I get the feeling that Fate is the primary Arcana for messing with the Arisen and things of an Iremite nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T22:28:53-08:00","id":805020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=804990#post804990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Set/Sutek, the Suzugoi of Fate, is either absent or roaming the cosmos with impunity. I get the feeling that Fate is the primary Arcana for messing with the Arisen and things of an Iremite nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. Especially when you have Ascended Deceived who are tied to Fate rather than a temakh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T22:41:57-08:00","id":805027,"title":"","content":"It has me wondering about the viability of an Acanthus as a scholar of all things Nameless Empire. He may need to splash for Death (to speak to ghosts and handle Lifeless), but Fate and Time seem like a very thematic pair for Mummy crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T02:05:58-08:00","id":805087,"title":"","content":"Duat is called &quot;the underworld&quot; in Mummy, but it's not the same as the Underworld from Geist, Mage, Demon, Promethean, and the core ghost rules. Yes, this is a bit confusing.<br /> <br /> Mummies also think of Death-aspected Twilight, the state ghosts in the material world are in, as a realm (Nefer-Kehet) and say that Duat is beyond it. That's a angle of looking at the universe unique to Mummy, like the Skein in Changeling or the Primordial Dream in Beast. It's not *wrong*, it's just a way of looking at the cosmos that other supernatural beings don't share.<br /> <br /> More on this, as you'd expect, in the Mage/Mummy 16th Century Africa crossover in the Dark Eras Companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T03:16:49-08:00","id":805112,"title":"","content":"To maybe clarify a bit -<br /> <br /> Every other supernatural being (so far! Although I can't see Deviants much caring about it) see Twilight as a state of existence and the Underworld as a seperate Realm that's walled off from the material world but reached through Avernian gates.<br /> <br /> Mummies see Twilight as a Realm and the blue-book Underworld (tunnels, rivers, etc) as <i>part</i> of that realm, with Duat &quot;Westward&quot; from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T03:30:47-08:00","id":805118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=804924#post804924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they're the same as Mage's Lower Depths.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lower Depths from Mage don't really have enough substance or reality to be anything at all. They're vague half-existent realities, mostly full of void and nothing. About all they have to offer is a hollow and empty hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T03:33:02-08:00","id":805119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=805112#post805112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummies see Twilight as a Realm and the blue-book Underworld (tunnels, rivers, etc) as <i>part</i> of that realm, with Duat &quot;Westward&quot; from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of the way Werewolves consider the Anima Mundi to be simply a deep and strange part of the Shadow, whereas Mages view the Astral and the Shadow as being entirely distinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6748,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","user":"Michael Kenner","date":".  Getting my terms mixed up. 01-10-2016, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T03:43:28-08:00","id":805122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=805112#post805112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummies see Twilight as a Realm and the blue-book Underworld (tunnels, rivers, etc) as <i>part</i> of that realm, with Duat &quot;Westward&quot; from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are Avernian Gates always considered &quot;open&quot; to Mummies (in Twilight, at least), then? It would explain why they see Twilight and the Underworld as one in the same, if they never encountered any kind of hard stop or border.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T03:45:08-08:00","id":805123,"title":"","content":"No, but it's like not considering the contents of a bank vault as being in another universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T03:45:45-08:00","id":805124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=805118#post805118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Lower Depths from Mage don't really have enough substance or reality to be anything at all. They're vague half-existent realities, mostly full of void and nothing. About all they have to offer is a hollow and empty hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Some are emptier than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T03:52:10-08:00","id":805128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/521150-making-crossover-work-for-mummy?p=805124#post805124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some are emptier than others.</div> </div> </div> </div>The really creepy thing is that I'm not sure whether being empt